endobj
52 0 obj<</ActualText( ’challenges  AND design decision)/K[43]/P 107 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
53 0 obj<</ActualText(Challenges)/K[44]/P 108 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
54 0 obj<</ActualText(The main challenges were presenting a large amount of organizational information without making the website feel overwhelming, creating a strong motorcycle-focused visual identity, and organizing different activities and programmes into a clear structure.\nAnother challenge was balancing visual storytelling with usability, ensuring that large images and bold sections did not distract users from important information and actions.)/K[45]/P 109 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
55 0 obj<</ActualText(Decision Outcomes)/K[46]/P 110 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
56 0 obj<</ActualText(To address these challenges, I created a clear navigation structure for quick access to important sections and used a strong hero section to immediately communicate the organization's identity. I grouped the organization's core values into three simple sections, used programme cards to make activities easy to scan, and added real event photography to create authenticity and strengthen the sense of community. Clear CTA buttons such as Join Us and Register encourage user engagement, while a dedicated contact form provides visitors with a direct communication channel.)/K[47]/P 111 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
57 0 obj<</ActualText( ’What i Learned)/K[48]/P 112 0 R/Pg 8 0 R/S/Span/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
58 0 obj<</K[49]/P 113 0 R/S/Span/Pg 8 0 R/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
